title: The Left SRs Break Away
subtitle: The party's left wing founds its own party.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: player_party = 'sr' and dix >= 22
priority: 20
max-visits: 1

= The Left SRs Break Away

In November the Left SRs, who have held their own congress, declared that the party's Central Committee no longer spoke for the peasants, and that they would form a party of their own. The Central Committee has expelled them for forming a separate organisation. The Left SRs have called a founding congress for early December: 116 delegates from 99 organisations. [? if bol_regime = 1 : Lenin has let it be known that there are seats in his government for them. ?]

The party's left wing is a part of its members, and nearly all of its voters in the Baltic Fleet, in the Petrograd garrison and in many a village.

- @reconcile: Reconcile with the Left SRs, and keep the party whole.
- @letgo: Let them go.

@reconcile
choose-if: intl_dissent < 45 and rel_lsr >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The Left SRs are too angry, or the party has not been listening.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_kept = 1;
Q.lsr_split = 0;
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -15);
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 6});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 3);
!}

A party conference gave the Left SRs the places they asked for on the Central Committee, a pledge to oppose the Treaty with Germany and the Bolshevik repression, and a promise of a Peasant Congress. The Left SRs withdrew their expulsion, and the party is, narrowly, whole.

@letgo
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_kept = 0;
Q.lsr_split = 1;
Q.intl_strength = Q.intl_strength * 0.3;
Q.intl_dissent = 0;
// the Left SRs are gone: what remains on the party's left is Chernov's Left Centre
Q.flabel_intl = 'The Left Centre'; Q.ilbl = 'the Left Centre'; Q.Ilbl = 'The Left Centre';
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: -10});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -4, soldiers: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, -6);
Q.members -= 20 * Q.mem_scale;
!}

The Left SRs held their founding congress and walked out of the party, taking the Baltic Fleet, the Petrograd garrison and a part of the villages. The party that remains is more united, and a good deal smaller.
